   1:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c **** /**
   2:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   ******************************************************************************
   3:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   * @file    stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c
   4:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   * @author  MCD Application Team
   5:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   * @brief   GPIO HAL module driver.
   6:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   *          This file provides firmware functions to manage the following 
   7:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   *          functionalities of the General Purpose Input/Output (GPIO) peripheral:
   8:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   *           + Initialization and de-initialization functions
   9:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   *           + IO operation functions
  10:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   *
  11:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   @verbatim
  12:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   ==============================================================================
  13:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****                     ##### GPIO Peripheral features #####
  14:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   ==============================================================================
  15:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   [..] 
  16:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   Subject to the specific hardware characteristics of each I/O port listed in the datasheet, each
  17:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   port bit of the General Purpose IO (GPIO) Ports, can be individually configured by software
  18:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   in several modes:
  19:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   (+) Input mode 
  20:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   (+) Analog mode
  21:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   (+) Output mode
  22:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   (+) Alternate function mode
  23:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   (+) External interrupt/event lines
  24:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  25:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   [..]  
  26:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   During and just after reset, the alternate functions and external interrupt  
  27:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   lines are not active and the I/O ports are configured in input floating mode.
  28:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   
  29:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   [..]   
  30:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   All GPIO pins have weak internal pull-up and pull-down resistors, which can be 
  31:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   activated or not.
  32:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  33:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   [..]
  34:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   In Output or Alternate mode, each IO can be configured on open-drain or push-pull
  35:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   type and the IO speed can be selected depending on the VDD value.
  36:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  37:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   [..]  
  38:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   All ports have external interrupt/event capability. To use external interrupt 
  39:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   lines, the port must be configured in input mode. All available GPIO pins are 
  40:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   connected to the 16 external interrupt/event lines from EXTI0 to EXTI15.
  41:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   
  42:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   [..]
  43:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   The external interrupt/event controller consists of up to 23 edge detectors 
  44:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   (16 lines are connected to GPIO) for generating event/interrupt requests (each 
  45:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   input line can be independently configured to select the type (interrupt or event) 
  46:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   and the corresponding trigger event (rising or falling or both). Each line can 
  47:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   also be masked independently. 
  48:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  49:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****                      ##### How to use this driver #####
  50:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   ==============================================================================  
  51:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   [..]
  52:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (#) Enable the GPIO AHB clock using the following function: __HAL_RCC_GPIOx_CLK_ENABLE(). 
  53:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  54:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (#) Configure the GPIO pin(s) using HAL_GPIO_Init().
  55:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) Configure the IO mode using "Mode" member from GPIO_InitTypeDef structure
  56:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) Activate Pull-up, Pull-down resistor using "Pull" member from GPIO_InitTypeDef 
  57:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****              structure.
  58:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) In case of Output or alternate function mode selection: the speed is 
  59:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****              configured through "Speed" member from GPIO_InitTypeDef structure.
  60:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) In alternate mode is selection, the alternate function connected to the IO
  61:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****              is configured through "Alternate" member from GPIO_InitTypeDef structure.
  62:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) Analog mode is required when a pin is to be used as ADC channel 
  63:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****              or DAC output.
  64:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) In case of external interrupt/event selection the "Mode" member from 
  65:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****              GPIO_InitTypeDef structure select the type (interrupt or event) and 
  66:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****              the corresponding trigger event (rising or falling or both).
  67:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  68:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (#) In case of external interrupt/event mode selection, configure NVIC IRQ priority 
  69:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****         mapped to the EXTI line using HAL_NVIC_SetPriority() and enable it using
  70:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****         HAL_NVIC_EnableIRQ().
  71:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****          
  72:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (#) To get the level of a pin configured in input mode use HAL_GPIO_ReadPin().
  73:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****             
  74:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (#) To set/reset the level of a pin configured in output mode use 
  75:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****         HAL_GPIO_WritePin()/HAL_GPIO_TogglePin().
  76:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****     
  77:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (#) To lock pin configuration until next reset use HAL_GPIO_LockPin().
  78:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  79:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****                  
  80:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (#) During and just after reset, the alternate functions are not 
  81:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****         active and the GPIO pins are configured in input floating mode (except JTAG
  82:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****         pins).
  83:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   
  84:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (#) The LSE oscillator pins OSC32_IN and OSC32_OUT can be used as general purpose 
  85:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****         (PC14 and PC15, respectively) when the LSE oscillator is off. The LSE has 
  86:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****         priority over the GPIO function.
  87:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   
  88:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (#) The HSE oscillator pins OSC_IN/OSC_OUT can be used as 
  89:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****         general purpose PH0 and PH1, respectively, when the HSE oscillator is off. 
  90:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****         The HSE has priority over the GPIO function.
  91:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   
  92:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   @endverbatim
  93:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   ******************************************************************************
  94:./src/stm32f7xx_hal_gpio.c ****   * @attention
